{"id":"c896047f-7708-4254-a1d2-bd01ca34aaba","revision":0,"last_node_id":30,"last_link_id":52,"nodes":[{"id":1,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[0,-400],"size":[2900,340],"flags":{},"order":0,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"properties":{},"widgets_values":["## Arbor · Character sheet — a three-level tree (Qwen Image 2.1 Turbo)\n\n**character → outfit → pose**, and the levels are uneven: Mira has three outfits, Theo two. A flat list can't hold this; a data tree can.\n\n1. **Characters** Panel: `# name` starts a character, the first line describes them, every further line is an outfit. → one named branch per character.\n2. **List Item** `0` takes each character's description, `1:` their outfits — per branch, all characters at once.\n3. **Cross Reference** (group on) gives every outfit its own sub-branch `{character;outfit}` holding every pose. The character branch becomes the parent and keeps its name, the sub-branch is named after the outfit → `Mira · red raincoat`.\n4. A second **Cross Reference** (outfits × descriptions, group on) hands each of those sub-branches its character's description — same branches, same order. Now **Expression** `y + \", wearing \" + x` simply pairs branch with branch, and the single description repeats for every pose (longest list) — Grasshopper's data matching. A second Expression adds the pose.\n5. **Tree to Data** flattens the 15 prompts for the sampler; the *structure* brings them back: one row per outfit (labelled `Mira · red raincoat`), and **Reshape Tree** *shift paths −1* folds the outfits back into one row per character (labelled `Mira`, `Theo`).\n\nAdd a character, an outfit or a pose — every count follows."],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"## Arbor · Character sheet — a three-level tree (Qwen Image 2.1 Turbo)\n\n**character → outfit → pose**, and the levels are uneven: Mira has three outfits, Theo two. A flat list can't hold this; a data tree can.\n\n1. **Characters** Panel: `# name` starts a character, the first line describes them, every further line is an outfit. → one named branch per character.\n2. **List Item** `0` takes each character's description, `1:` their outfits — per branch, all characters at once.\n3. **Cross Reference** (group on) gives every outfit its own sub-branch `{character;outfit}` holding every pose. The character branch becomes the parent and keeps its name, the sub-branch is named after the outfit → `Mira · red raincoat`.\n4. A second **Cross Reference** (outfits × descriptions, group on) hands each of those sub-branches its character's description — same branches, same order. Now **Expression** `y + \", wearing \" + x` simply pairs branch with branch, and the single description repeats for every pose (longest list) — Grasshopper's data matching. A second Expression adds the pose.\n5. **Tree to Data** flattens the 15 prompts for the sampler; the *structure* brings them back: one row per outfit (labelled `Mira · red raincoat`), and **Reshape Tree** *shift paths −1* folds the outfits back into one row per character (labelled `Mira`, `Theo`).\n\nAdd a character, an outfit or a pose — every count follows."},"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":2,"type":"Arbor_Panel","pos":[0,0],"size":[420,420],"flags":{},"order":1,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"数据","name":"data","shape":7,"type":"*","link":null},{"localized_name":"文本","name":"text","type":"STRING","widget":{"name":"text"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"识别数值","name":"parse_numbers","type":"BOOLEAN","widget":{"name":"parse_numbers"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"整段文本","name":"multiline","type":"BOOLEAN","widget":{"name":"multiline"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"数据","name":"data","shape":6,"type":"*","links":null},{"localized_name":"数据树","name":"tree","type":"ARBOR_TREE","links":[1,2]}],"title":"Characters","properties":{"Node name for S&R":"Arbor_Panel"},"widgets_values":["# Mira\na young botanist with short silver hair and freckles\nred raincoat with a canvas satchel\nwhite lab coat with pinn